634
00:27:55.810 --> 00:27:58.130
And then I did a weird mini dive.
然后我做了一个小小的深度挖掘。

635
00:27:58.730 --> 00:27:59.210
All right.
好吧。

636
00:27:59.330 --> 00:28:00.150
I want you to see.
我想让你看看。

637
00:28:00.350 --> 00:28:01.270
I'll put this in stories.
我会把它发到快拍里。

638
00:28:01.450 --> 00:28:02.090
But you got to see.
但你一定要看看。

639
00:28:02.230 --> 00:28:02.810
Look at your nails.
看看你的指甲。

640
00:28:03.730 --> 00:28:05.590
How did I get away with that?
我是怎么蒙混过关的？

641
00:28:05.990 --> 00:28:07.510
Why did they let me do that?
他们为什么让我那样做？

642
00:28:08.010 --> 00:28:09.150
I don't know.
我不知道。

643
00:28:09.150 --> 00:28:19.310
Because I will just say that if I ever came in with a nail polish that wasn't a natural looking nail polish, they would make me take it off in the trailer in the morning.
因为我只想说，如果我哪天涂了那种看起来不自然的指甲油来上班，他们早上在化妆车里就会让我把它卸掉。

644
00:28:19.310 --> 00:28:25.190
I don't know how this fell through the cracks, but I remember this nail polish on you.
我不知道这怎么成了漏网之鱼，但我记得你涂过这种指甲油。

645
00:28:25.310 --> 00:28:26.310
Is this so weird?
这不是很奇怪吗？

646
00:28:26.670 --> 00:28:27.670
What is it?
那是什么？

647
00:28:27.830 --> 00:28:36.290
I looked up on the internet and it said in the fall of 2008, one of the big trends in nail polish was gray nail polish.
我在网上查了一下，上面说2008年秋天，指甲油的一大流行趋势是灰色指甲油。

648
00:28:36.290 --> 00:28:47.910
In fact, collegecandy.com said the OPI Sephora had a very popular color called Metro Chic, which was a matte purplish gray.
事实上，collegecandy.com网站说OPI丝芙兰有一款非常受欢迎的颜色叫Metro Chic，是一种哑光的紫灰色。

649
00:28:48.330 --> 00:28:50.090
Well, I think we all know.
好吧，我想我们都知道。

650
00:28:50.450 --> 00:28:52.290
If anything, I'm on trend.
至少，我紧跟潮流。

651
00:28:52.890 --> 00:28:54.490
Hey, you know the fashions.
嘿，你很懂时尚嘛。

652
00:28:54.630 --> 00:28:55.090
I do.
我懂。

653
00:28:55.330 --> 00:28:56.610
I really do.
我是真的懂。

654
00:28:57.030 --> 00:29:00.610
I think you got some Metro Chic and put it on your nails for the weekend.
我觉得你周末涂了点“都市时尚”色指甲油。

655
00:29:00.770 --> 00:29:01.890
I have no doubt.
我对此深信不疑。

656
00:29:02.230 --> 00:29:02.370
Someone didn't catch it.
有人没发现。

657
00:29:02.510 --> 00:29:04.370
I love OPI nail polish.
我超爱OPI的指甲油。

658
00:29:04.530 --> 00:29:05.570
I wear it all the time.
我一直都在用。

659
00:29:05.570 --> 00:29:07.210
I am certain that's what it was.
我敢肯定就是那个颜色。

660
00:29:07.610 --> 00:29:09.410
I just can't believe I got away with it.
我真不敢相信我竟然蒙混过关了。

661
00:29:09.530 --> 00:29:15.450
You know, they would let Amy Ryan and Melora Harden, as their characters, they could have a darker nail polish.
你知道，他们会让艾米·莱恩和梅洛拉·哈登饰演的角色涂深色指甲油。

662
00:29:15.450 --> 00:29:21.690
But they wanted Pam to always, like, either have no nail polish or just some clear nail polish.
但他们希望帕姆总是要么不涂指甲油，要么只涂透明的。

663
00:29:22.070 --> 00:29:23.670
I sneaked it in, I guess.
我想我是偷偷涂上的。

664
00:29:24.050 --> 00:29:27.270
Maybe I sat on my hands while I got my hair and makeup done that day.
也许那天做头发和化妆的时候，我一直把手压在屁股底下。

665
00:29:27.630 --> 00:29:32.230
Well, listen, Andy's going to come in and he's clearly upset about something.
听着，安迪要进来了，他显然因为某事心烦意乱。

666
00:29:32.550 --> 00:29:35.030
He would like to address the elephant in the room.
他想谈谈那个显而易见却被大家刻意回避的问题。

667
00:29:35.370 --> 00:29:41.550
I love how Rainn Wilson, as Dwight, chose to kind of stand up and get in a power stance.
我很喜欢雷恩·威尔森饰演的德怀特，他选择站起来摆出一个强势的姿态。

668
00:29:41.550 --> 00:29:42.230
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

669
00:29:42.350 --> 00:29:48.210
He's ready to fight because, of course, we all think that he knows about this affair that Angela's having with Dwight.
他准备好要打架了，因为我们当然都以为他知道安吉拉和德怀特有私情的事。

670
00:29:48.910 --> 00:29:50.390
But that's not what he says.
但那并不是他要说的。

671
00:29:50.790 --> 00:29:53.670
He says, none of you have RSVP'd to our wedding.
他说，你们谁都没回复我们的婚礼请柬。

672
00:29:54.230 --> 00:29:55.010
How awkward.
太尴尬了。

673
00:29:55.410 --> 00:30:04.470
In the deleted scenes, this scene goes on where he goes to every single person and is like, hey, Phyllis, you haven't RSVP'd Jim.
在删减片段里，这一幕还有后续，他走到每个人面前说，嘿，菲利斯，你还没回复吉姆呢。

674
00:30:04.470 --> 00:30:06.790
And everyone, like, pretends to be on the phone.
然后每个人都假装在打电话。

675
00:30:06.930 --> 00:30:07.490
Oh, no.
噢，不。

676
00:30:07.710 --> 00:30:14.510
You have this hilarious talking head where you're, like, you say you've been avoiding him and you can't look him in the eye, so you only look at his nose.
你有个超搞笑的采访镜头，你说你一直在躲着他，不敢看他的眼睛，所以只能盯着他的鼻子看。

677
00:30:15.730 --> 00:30:21.650
So then Andy comes up to you and asks you and you're just awkwardly looking at his nose and then he thinks he has something on his nose.
然后安迪走过来问你，你就尴尬地盯着他的鼻子看，结果他以为自己鼻子上沾了什么东西。

678
00:30:21.810 --> 00:30:23.170
It was really funny.
真的太搞笑了。

679
00:30:23.350 --> 00:30:28.470
The deleted scenes for this episode, I feel like every single one of them should have been in because they were all awesome.
我觉得这一集的每一个删减片段都应该保留，因为它们都太棒了。

680
00:30:29.190 --> 00:30:32.470
Oh, Jim says it's been 17 days.
噢，吉姆说已经过去17天了。

681
00:30:32.710 --> 00:30:38.230
It's been 17 days since the Christmas party when Phyllis spilled the beans.
距离菲利斯说漏嘴的那场圣诞派对已经过去17天了。

682
00:30:38.630 --> 00:30:44.350
Everyone meets in the break room except Andy and Michael says he's going to tell him.
除了安迪，大家都在休息室集合，迈克尔说他要去告诉安迪。

683
00:30:44.570 --> 00:30:45.590
He has to tell him.
他必须告诉他。

684
00:30:46.130 --> 00:30:46.510
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

685
00:30:46.910 --> 00:30:49.450
And, of course, everyone's like, you can't.
当然，大家都说，你不能这么做。

686
00:30:49.570 --> 00:30:51.090
It's really Angela's responsibility.
这其实是安吉拉的责任。

687
00:30:51.530 --> 00:30:51.950
Oh.
噢。

688
00:30:52.210 --> 00:30:55.270
And then I loved the exchange between Oscar and Dwight.
还有，我超爱奥斯卡和德怀特之间的那段对话。

689
00:30:55.390 --> 00:30:56.470
Oh, I know.
噢，我知道。

690
00:30:56.470 --> 00:30:59.170
I was anticipating it as you were about to say it.
在你还没说出口时，我就已经预料到了。

691
00:30:59.310 --> 00:31:06.870
And just the fact that the whole group starts learning where all Angela and Dwight have shagged in the office.
而且大家开始了解到安吉拉和德怀特在办公室里所有发生过亲密关系的地方，这事实本身就很有趣。

692
00:31:09.130 --> 00:31:11.670
We had a fan question from Jess R.
我们收到了杰斯·R发来的粉丝提问，

693
00:31:11.930 --> 00:31:13.070
who said,
他问道，

694
00:31:13.750 --> 00:31:21.390
Who wrote the moment in the break room when Dwight implies he's been doing it with Angela on Oscar's desk and was any of that scene improvised?
休息室里德怀特暗示他和安吉拉在奥斯卡的桌子上做过那事的桥段是谁写的？那一幕有即兴发挥吗？

695
00:31:22.050 --> 00:31:22.650
No.
没有。

696
00:31:23.010 --> 00:31:24.230
None of it was improvised.
完全没有即兴发挥。

697
00:31:24.230 --> 00:31:26.730
It was all scripted by Jen Salata.
全是珍·萨拉塔写的剧本。

698
00:31:27.410 --> 00:31:28.150
So good.
写得太好了。

699
00:31:30.130 --> 00:31:35.130
This scene takes us into accounting, and Angela's kind of giving it to Kevin that he's screwed up again.
这一幕把我们带到了会计部，安吉拉正在数落凯文，说他又搞砸了。

700
00:31:35.410 --> 00:31:37.400
And then there's some real Kevin sass.
然后凯文展现了真正的毒舌一面。

701
00:31:38.070 --> 00:31:39.230
Oh, it's great.
噢，太棒了。

702
00:31:39.510 --> 00:31:40.320
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

703
00:31:40.750 --> 00:31:43.790
He's like, I didn't realize I was doing something wrong.
他当时就像是，我没意识到我做错了什么。

704
00:31:43.790 --> 00:31:46.470
If I had, I would have admitted it and stopped right away.
如果我知道的话，我早就承认并立刻停止了。

705
00:31:46.770 --> 00:31:48.810
He really leans in hard on this moment.
他真的非常投入这一刻。

706
00:31:49.110 --> 00:31:50.790
And Oscar gives him props.
奥斯卡还夸了他。

707
00:31:50.970 --> 00:31:52.150
He's like, no, that was really good.
奥斯卡就像是，不，那真的很棒。

708
00:31:52.150 --> 00:31:53.010
You did a great job.
你做得很好。

709
00:31:53.210 --> 00:31:53.610
Congratulations.
恭喜你。

710
00:31:55.110 --> 00:32:02.030
Jenna, immediately after the scene in the script, there's a very angry Angela talking head.
珍娜，剧本里那场戏之后紧接着就是安吉拉非常愤怒的个人访谈。

711
00:32:02.030 --> 00:32:13.810
And it's pretty amazing because Angela is so furious that she breaks the fourth wall and berates the camera documentary crew and then flashes them some of her shoulder.
而且这非常惊人，因为安吉拉气到打破了第四面墙，斥责了纪录片摄制组，还向他们露出了肩膀。

712
00:32:14.190 --> 00:32:14.710
Really?
真的吗？

713
00:32:15.370 --> 00:32:17.450
Yes, Sam, will you play it?
是的，山姆，你能放一下吗？

714
00:32:18.050 --> 00:32:22.250
It's just so important for you to get your big story, isn't it?
你们非得挖出什么大新闻才行，是吧？

715
00:32:22.610 --> 00:32:25.970
To edit everything together to make it look like there's a villain.
把所有素材剪辑在一起，好让看起来有个反派。

716
00:32:26.670 --> 00:32:28.730
Well, there's not always a villain.
好吧，并不总是会有反派。

717
00:32:29.310 --> 00:32:36.210
Sometimes there's just a hardworking, petite woman trying to make a conscientious decision about the rest of her life.
有时只是一个努力工作、娇小的女人，试图为自己的余生做出一个慎重的决定。

718
00:32:36.710 --> 00:32:37.610
Too boring?
太无聊了？

719
00:32:38.110 --> 00:32:39.270
Did I lose you?
我让你感到无聊了吗？

720
00:32:40.630 --> 00:32:41.210
Here.
给。

721
00:32:41.550 --> 00:32:42.710
Is this what you want?
这是你们想要的吗？

722
00:32:43.950 --> 00:32:45.470
Okay, that was amazing.
好吧，那太精彩了。

723
00:32:45.470 --> 00:32:55.950
But I have to say, I think it was right to cut it out because I don't know if we've ever had that much direct conversation with the documentary crew before.
但我不得不说，我认为剪掉它是对的，因为我不确定我们之前是否曾与纪录片摄制组有过这么多直接的对话。

724
00:32:56.170 --> 00:32:59.050
If we've ever referred so much to what they're doing.
我不确定我们是否曾如此频繁地提及他们的工作。

725
00:32:59.410 --> 00:33:01.870
I was shocked when I watched it, Jenna.
珍娜，我看到的时候惊呆了。

726
00:33:02.130 --> 00:33:03.510
Because she's like, is that what you want?
因为她当时就像是，这就是你们想要的吗？

727
00:33:03.570 --> 00:33:04.650
You're going to edit this together.
你们打算把这些剪辑在一起。

728
00:33:04.770 --> 00:33:05.610
You're going to make a villain.
你们打算塑造一个反派。

729
00:33:05.610 --> 00:33:15.490
And also, it was a little bit too sophisticated for Angela Martin to understand the whole process of a documentary and how they tell it through narration in these moments.
而且，让安吉拉·马丁去理解纪录片的整个制作过程，以及他们如何在这些时刻通过叙述来讲述故事，这稍微有点太复杂了。

730
00:33:15.730 --> 00:33:17.650
So I think it was the right move to cut it.
所以我认为剪掉它是正确的决定。

731
00:33:17.770 --> 00:33:19.430
But I was shocked when I saw it.
但我看到的时候确实很震惊。

732
00:33:19.510 --> 00:33:20.090
I had to share.
我必须分享一下。

733
00:33:20.090 --> 00:33:21.090
So Angela,
所以，安吉拉，

734
00:33:21.310 --> 00:33:33.830
I love this episode because there's just so much tension and it plays out so slowly over when or whether or not Andy is going to figure out that Angela's having an affair.
我喜欢这一集，因为里面充满了张力，而且安迪是否会发现安吉拉在搞外遇这件事，铺垫得非常缓慢。

735
00:33:34.350 --> 00:33:41.270
So he has this exclamation on the phone and everyone's like, but it's really just about the cake.
所以他在电话里有那样的惊呼，大家都以为出了什么事，但其实只是关于蛋糕的问题。

736
00:33:41.510 --> 00:33:43.430
He's just having an issue with the cake.
他只是在蛋糕上出了点问题。

737
00:33:43.430 --> 00:33:48.610
But this leads to that Dwight talking head because Dwight is on guard this whole time.
但这引出了德怀特的个人访谈，因为德怀特全程都处于戒备状态。

738
00:33:48.750 --> 00:33:50.570
He's like constantly leaping out of his chair.
他就像是不断地从椅子上跳起来。

739
00:33:51.450 --> 00:33:57.650
And he kind of explains that there are these 40 rules that all shroop boys must learn by the age of five.
他解释说，所有的施鲁特男孩在五岁前都必须学习40条规则。

740
00:33:57.830 --> 00:34:03.690
And one of these rules is like, don't put your back to a man who you've wronged.
其中一条规则是，不要背对着你亏待过的人。

741
00:34:04.290 --> 00:34:05.970
That's just one of the 40 rules.
那只是40条规则中的一条。

742
00:34:06.750 --> 00:34:11.030
Don't turn your back on a bear or a dominant turkey during mating season.
不要背对着熊，或者交配季节里占主导地位的火鸡。

743
00:34:11.030 --> 00:34:14.150
Yeah, there's a lot of things you shouldn't turn your back on.
是的，有很多东西你都不应该背对着。

744
00:34:14.390 --> 00:34:16.850
And then he has this little jingle that he sings.
然后他唱了一段小曲子。

745
00:34:17.230 --> 00:34:22.470
Now, Angela, is it true that Rain improvised that song?
那么，安吉拉，雷恩即兴创作了那首歌是真的吗？

746
00:34:22.850 --> 00:34:24.310
Oh, no, that was in the script.
噢，不，那是剧本里写的。

747
00:34:24.550 --> 00:34:25.690
That was 100% written.
那是百分之百写好的。

748
00:34:26.130 --> 00:34:30.530
They shared in the DVD commentary that Rain was singing the jingle a few different ways.
他们在DVD评论音轨里分享说，雷恩当时试着唱了几种不同版本的小曲。

749
00:34:30.810 --> 00:34:34.150
And then Dean asked Jen, Jen, how did you hear it when you wrote it?
然后迪恩问简，简，你写的时候是怎么构思这段旋律的？

750
00:34:34.350 --> 00:34:37.290
She sort of sang it her way and they found it in the moment.
她就用自己的方式唱了一下，他们当时就定下来了。

751
00:34:37.550 --> 00:34:39.830
So they found the melody, but the words were written.
所以他们找到了旋律，但歌词是写好的。

752
00:34:39.830 --> 00:34:41.670
The words are totally written.
歌词完全是写好的。

753
00:34:42.010 --> 00:34:42.650
They're in the script.
都在剧本里。

754
00:34:42.850 --> 00:34:44.850
This is like fabulous Jen Salata writing.
这就像是詹·萨拉塔写的精彩剧本。

755
00:34:45.130 --> 00:34:47.150
They just improvised the melody.
他们只是即兴创作了旋律。

756
00:34:47.750 --> 00:34:48.210
Got it.
明白了。

757
00:34:48.450 --> 00:34:53.070
Well, now Dwight is going to signal Angela to meet him in the hallway.
好了，现在德怀特要示意安吉拉去走廊见他。

758
00:34:53.470 --> 00:34:57.750
He does this by moving his little bobblehead to the other side of his desk.
他通过把他的小摇头娃娃移到办公桌的另一边来做到这一点。

759
00:34:58.150 --> 00:34:58.710
Yes.
是的。

760
00:34:58.990 --> 00:35:00.490
He's going to confront her.
他要去找她对质。

761
00:35:00.770 --> 00:35:03.150
He wants her to tell Andy the truth.
他想让她告诉安迪真相。

762
00:35:04.470 --> 00:35:07.550
And Angela has a line, Jenna, that really made me laugh.
而且安吉拉有一句台词，珍娜，真的让我笑了。

763
00:35:07.650 --> 00:35:09.230
She's like, this is a terrible idea.
她说，这真是个糟糕的主意。

764
00:35:09.230 --> 00:35:10.210
One of your worSt.
你最糟糕的主意之一。

765
00:35:10.410 --> 00:35:11.890
And then he's like, just get it over with.
然后他说，快点结束吧。

766
00:35:12.030 --> 00:35:16.170
And then Angela says, you're expanding on your worst idea.
接着安吉拉说，你正在把你最糟糕的主意发扬光大。

767
00:35:16.770 --> 00:35:18.570
That just really made me laugh.
那真的让我笑了。

768
00:35:19.030 --> 00:35:22.970
Well, Michael is leaving now and he asks Andy to walk with him.
好了，迈克尔现在要离开了，他让安迪陪他走一段。

769
00:35:23.230 --> 00:35:23.670
Yeah.
是的。

770
00:35:23.750 --> 00:35:24.690
He's going to do it.
他要这么做了。

771
00:35:24.870 --> 00:35:25.830
He's going to do it.
他要这么做了。

772
00:35:26.050 --> 00:35:27.510
He can't not do it.
他不可能不做。

773
00:35:27.630 --> 00:35:28.690
This is like true, Michael.
这真的很迈克尔。

774
00:35:28.810 --> 00:35:29.770
Like he can't not.
就像他无法拒绝一样。

775
00:35:30.210 --> 00:35:31.630
The scene is so funny.
这一幕太搞笑了。

776
00:35:31.970 --> 00:35:32.970
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

777
00:35:32.970 --> 00:35:35.410
I mean, it's so perfect.
我是说，太完美了。

778
00:35:35.930 --> 00:35:44.310
You know, I believe Angela originally in the scene, he is supposed to tell Andy before he got in his car.
你知道，我相信安吉拉最初在这一幕里，他本应该在进车前告诉安迪。

779
00:35:44.730 --> 00:35:45.290
Yes.
是的。

780
00:35:45.390 --> 00:35:47.810
It's scripted that he tells him outside of the car.
剧本里写的是他在车外告诉他。

781
00:35:47.970 --> 00:35:53.950
But on the day they came up with the idea that it would be really funny if Michael was in the car.
但在拍摄当天，他们想出了一个主意，如果迈克尔在车里会非常有趣。

782
00:35:54.090 --> 00:35:57.910
And then he sort of says it through the window as he's driving away.
然后他开车离开时，隔着窗户说了出来。

783
00:35:57.910 --> 00:35:59.250
And that is so good.
那真是太棒了。

784
00:35:59.250 --> 00:35:59.670
Yes.
是的。

785
00:35:59.850 --> 00:36:05.470
So in the commentary, Dean said he had the idea in the moment that the scene takes place with Michael in the car.
所以在评论音轨里，迪恩说他在那一刻想到了让迈克尔在车里拍摄这一幕的主意。

786
00:36:05.610 --> 00:36:10.110
And then Steve sort of built on that and was like, what if Michael really doesn't want to tell him?
然后史蒂夫在此基础上发挥，说，如果迈克尔真的不想告诉他会怎样？

787
00:36:10.210 --> 00:36:11.750
So it's kind of like as he's pulling away.
所以就像他正要开车离开时那样。

788
00:36:12.010 --> 00:36:16.130
And then Dean said that Steve really peeled out of the parking lot.
然后迪恩说史蒂夫真的猛踩油门冲出了停车场。

789
00:36:16.310 --> 00:36:18.710
They did not add that sound in in poSt.
他们并没有在后期制作中添加那个声音。

790
00:36:18.850 --> 00:36:20.750
That's actually the car peeling away.
那实际上就是车轮打滑的声音。

791
00:36:20.870 --> 00:36:21.950
Oh, that's amazing.
哦，那太神奇了。

792
00:36:22.430 --> 00:36:25.570
Well, we had a fan question from Maria M about this scene.
好了，我们收到了玛丽亚·M关于这一幕的粉丝提问。

793
00:36:26.070 --> 00:36:33.210
She said, is there a production-related reason why the vehicles in this episode all appear so dusty and dirty?
她问，这一集里的车辆看起来都那么灰头土脸、脏兮兮的，有什么制作上的原因吗？

794
00:36:33.670 --> 00:36:37.750
And when I went back and looked at it, yes, they're all covered in grime.
当我回去看的时候，确实，它们都覆盖着污垢。

795
00:36:37.970 --> 00:36:39.010
Yeah, they're filthy.
是的，它们脏透了。

796
00:36:39.010 --> 00:36:43.890
I asked Randy Cordray about it, and he said, yes, Maria.
我问了兰迪·科德雷，他说，是的，玛丽亚。

797
00:36:44.750 --> 00:36:46.430
Great eye to detail.
观察力真敏锐。

798
00:36:46.770 --> 00:36:52.630
All of the cars were purposely dirtied by the scenic painting crew using flour and water.
所有的车都是布景绘画组用面粉和水故意弄脏的。

799
00:36:52.650 --> 00:37:01.330
And this was meant to simulate what cars might look like during a typical Scranton winter from just road grime and salt.
这是为了模拟斯克兰顿典型的冬天里，汽车因为路面污垢和盐分可能呈现的样子。

800
00:37:02.050 --> 00:37:02.890
And snow.
还有雪。

801
00:37:03.130 --> 00:37:03.590
Yes.
是的。

802
00:37:03.590 --> 00:37:05.910
When snow gets dirty looking, right?
当雪看起来变脏的时候，对吧？

803
00:37:06.070 --> 00:37:07.030
And it's on your car.
而且还在你的车上。

804
00:37:07.410 --> 00:37:07.750
Yes.
是的。

805
00:37:07.990 --> 00:37:11.910
And that the cars in the parking lot belonged to our crew members.
停车场里的车都是我们剧组成员的。

806
00:37:11.910 --> 00:37:17.150
And any crew member who volunteered to park their car in the lot got a free car wash every Friday.
任何自愿把车停在停车场里的剧组成员，每周五都能免费洗一次车。

807
00:37:17.470 --> 00:37:18.670
Oh, how about that?
哦，那还不错吧？

808
00:37:18.810 --> 00:37:21.590
So during the week, they'd have to drive around with a grimy car.
所以在一周里，他们得开着脏兮兮的车到处跑。

809
00:37:21.750 --> 00:37:24.170
But on the weekends, you got a fresh, clean car.
但到了周末，你就能拥有一辆崭新干净的车了。

810
00:37:25.470 --> 00:37:29.330
Well, I think this is a good place to take a break because Andy knows the truth.
嗯，我觉得这里是个休息的好地方，因为安迪知道真相。

811
00:37:29.550 --> 00:37:32.170
And when we come back, we'll talk about what he does.
等我们回来，再聊聊他做了什么。

812
00:37:32.790 --> 00:37:33.730
Oh, man.
天哪。

813
00:37:34.130 --> 00:37:34.950
It's a lot.
这信息量太大了。

814
00:37:35.130 --> 00:37:37.570
This was some cringy stuff to watch.
看这些内容真是让人尴尬。

815
00:37:37.910 --> 00:37:38.870
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

816
00:37:48.800 --> 00:37:49.340
All right.
好的。

817
00:37:49.440 --> 00:37:50.240
We are back.
我们回来了。

818
00:37:50.500 --> 00:37:53.700
And guys, Meredith knew something big was going to happen today.
伙计们，梅雷迪思知道今天会有大事发生。

819
00:37:54.080 --> 00:37:58.880
Now, she said that yesterday, but she was also right yesterday because her neighbor was murdered.
虽然她昨天也这么说，但她昨天确实说对了，因为她的邻居被谋杀了。

820
00:37:59.140 --> 00:37:59.980
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

821
00:38:00.280 --> 00:38:01.060
What is her life?
她过的是什么生活啊？

822
00:38:03.480 --> 00:38:05.320
Like, throwaway lines.
就像是随口一提的台词。

823
00:38:05.520 --> 00:38:06.280
It's like her and Creed.
就像她和克里德一样。

824
00:38:06.480 --> 00:38:07.640
Like, what the heck is their life?
天呐，他们到底过的是什么生活？

825
00:38:07.780 --> 00:38:09.220
It must have been so fun to write for them.
给他们写剧本一定很有趣。

826
00:38:09.440 --> 00:38:10.040
I know.
我知道。

827
00:38:10.440 --> 00:38:15.920
At 8 minutes, 42 seconds, we get a really good shot of Meredith in this episode.
在8分42秒时，这一集里有一个梅雷迪思的特写镜头。

828
00:38:15.920 --> 00:38:18.880
And she is wearing a sweater veSt.
她穿着一件毛衣背心。

829
00:38:19.460 --> 00:38:20.020
Yes.
是的。

830
00:38:20.700 --> 00:38:27.100
Lady, I wore that same sweater vest to a press event with John Krasinski in New York.
天哪，我和约翰·卡拉辛斯基在纽约参加新闻发布会时，穿的就是那件同款毛衣背心。

831
00:38:27.400 --> 00:38:27.960
What?
什么？

832
00:38:28.280 --> 00:38:28.840
Yeah.
是啊。

833
00:38:29.000 --> 00:38:31.600
I walked on set this week.
这周我走进片场时。

834
00:38:31.600 --> 00:38:37.160
We were shooting The Duel, and I looked at Kate dressed as Meredith, and I thought, oh,
我们当时正在拍《决斗》那一集，我看到凯特打扮成梅雷迪思的样子，心想，哦，

835
00:38:37.240 --> 00:38:37.700
my God.
天哪。

836
00:38:38.720 --> 00:38:39.780
Oh, my God.
天哪。

837
00:38:39.940 --> 00:38:41.560
Did I make a terrible mistake?
我是不是犯了个大错？

838
00:38:41.560 --> 00:38:42.980
I thought it was fashionable.
我当时还觉得挺时尚的。

839
00:38:43.660 --> 00:38:51.080
I wore that same vest over this, like, big, poofy white blouse with big, poofy shoulders.
我把那件背心穿在一件又大又蓬的白色衬衫外面，肩膀那里也是蓬蓬的。

840
00:38:51.080 --> 00:38:52.360
This was the style.
当时就流行这个。

841
00:38:52.640 --> 00:38:53.000
What?
什么？

842
00:38:53.000 --> 00:38:55.860
It was actually a really expensive veSt.
那其实是一件很贵的背心。

843
00:38:56.020 --> 00:38:57.780
It was like Betsy Johnson or something.
好像是贝齐·约翰逊之类的牌子。

844
00:38:58.380 --> 00:39:01.520
Can we do a side-by-side of you and Meredith?
我们能把你和梅雷迪思的照片放在一起对比一下吗？

845
00:39:01.840 --> 00:39:02.340
We muSt.
必须得放。

846
00:39:02.720 --> 00:39:08.020
Jenna, in real life, has the same fashion choices as Meredith.
珍娜在现实生活中的时尚品味竟然和梅雷迪思一样。

847
00:39:08.300 --> 00:39:08.880
Lady, look.
天哪，你看。

848
00:39:08.960 --> 00:39:09.560
Here's a picture.
这是照片。

849
00:39:09.680 --> 00:39:10.220
Look at it.
你看。

850
00:39:13.180 --> 00:39:13.700
See?
看到了吗？

851
00:39:14.040 --> 00:39:16.400
Look at it.
你看这个。

852
00:39:16.480 --> 00:39:17.200
Oh, my God.
天哪。

853
00:39:17.200 --> 00:39:20.380
First of all, you and John look 14 years old.
首先，你和约翰看起来才14岁。

854
00:39:20.520 --> 00:39:22.900
We have to put this photo in Office Ladies Stories.
我们得把这张照片放进《办公室》幕后故事里。

855
00:39:23.160 --> 00:39:28.720
You are wearing Meredith's sweater vest, and John looks like he could host Blue's Clues.
你穿着梅雷迪思的毛衣背心，约翰看起来就像能去主持《蓝狗线索》一样。

856
00:39:29.160 --> 00:39:30.100
He does.
确实像。

857
00:39:30.220 --> 00:39:32.440
He's in, like, a stripy polo.
他穿得像件条纹Polo衫。

858
00:39:32.640 --> 00:39:32.820
Yeah.
没错。

859
00:39:32.960 --> 00:39:33.320
Oh, my God.
天哪。

860
00:39:33.320 --> 00:39:34.500
You guys look 14 years old.
你们看起来才14岁。

861
00:39:34.580 --> 00:39:41.720
We were doing press at this NBC Experience store, showing off all the new Office merchandise.
当时我们在NBC体验店做宣传，展示所有新的《办公室》周边商品。

862
00:39:42.180 --> 00:39:43.020
Meredith called.
梅雷迪思打来电话。

863
00:39:43.200 --> 00:39:44.520
She wants her sweater vest back.
她想要回她的毛衣背心。

864
00:39:44.520 --> 00:39:45.580
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

865
00:39:46.680 --> 00:39:50.220
And, like, I'd already done the event, you know?
而且，你知道，我已经参加完活动了。

866
00:39:51.100 --> 00:39:56.840
Well, you could have heard a pin drop when Andy walked back into that bullpen, and he
安迪走回办公区时，现场安静得连根针掉在地上都能听见，然后他

867
00:39:56.840 --> 00:39:59.580
goes over to Angela and says, we need to talk.
走到安吉拉面前说，我们需要谈谈。

868
00:39:59.740 --> 00:40:01.180
And she's like, we can talk right here.
她说，我们就在这儿谈吧。

869
00:40:01.400 --> 00:40:03.080
And he's like, no, no.
他说，不，不行。

870
00:40:03.840 --> 00:40:05.240
Ed played it so real.
艾德演得太真实了。

871
00:40:05.700 --> 00:40:06.240
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

872
00:40:06.700 --> 00:40:07.820
I was sweating.
我当时都在冒汗。

873
00:40:08.160 --> 00:40:09.140
I was sweating it.
我紧张得直冒汗。

874
00:40:09.300 --> 00:40:10.180
Like, I felt it.
我感同身受。

875
00:40:10.580 --> 00:40:13.060
We went to that conference room, and he shut the door.
我们去了会议室，他关上了门。

876
00:40:13.060 --> 00:40:16.120
And we were in there a long time.
我们在里面待了很久。

877
00:40:17.440 --> 00:40:19.460
And Ed broke my heart.
艾德让我心碎了。

878
00:40:20.220 --> 00:40:20.920
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

879
00:40:21.840 --> 00:40:24.860
As Andy, when he was like, do you love him?
作为安迪，当他说出“你爱他吗？”的时候。

880
00:40:25.460 --> 00:40:25.980
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

881
00:40:26.440 --> 00:40:29.280
And I was really feeling all of this emotion.
我当时真的感受到了所有这些情绪。

882
00:40:30.100 --> 00:40:34.860
And then Angela has to make this plea, this plea to him to don't give up on us.
然后安吉拉必须向他恳求，恳求他不要放弃我们。

883
00:40:35.700 --> 00:40:44.360
And, Jenna, it was all going great until we got to two words, formal chrysanthemuMs.
珍娜，一切都很顺利，直到我们说到两个词：正式的菊花。

884
00:40:46.180 --> 00:40:47.260
I couldn't say it.
我根本说不出来。

885
00:40:47.660 --> 00:40:48.660
Formal chrysanthemuMs.
正式的菊花。

886
00:40:52.700 --> 00:40:53.500
Formal chrysanthemuMs.
正式的菊花。

887
00:40:53.600 --> 00:40:57.380
I really had to break it down to be able to say it.
我真的必须把它拆解开才能说出来。

888
00:40:57.460 --> 00:40:59.560
But you need to say it like it's effortless.
但你得说得好像毫不费力一样。

889
00:40:59.720 --> 00:41:01.800
But I literally was like going formal.
但我当时真的就是那种，正式。

890
00:41:03.080 --> 00:41:03.480
ChrysanthemuMs.
菊花。

891
00:41:04.040 --> 00:41:04.940
You know what, lady?
你知道吗，女士？

892
00:41:05.180 --> 00:41:09.140
That is not anything having to do with your accent or you.
这跟你的口音或者你本人一点关系都没有。

893
00:41:09.320 --> 00:41:10.720
I challenge anyone to say that word.
我敢挑战任何人去说那个词。

894
00:41:10.880 --> 00:41:11.160
I can't.
我做不到。

895
00:41:11.700 --> 00:41:12.180
ChrysanthemuMs.
菊花。

896
00:41:12.500 --> 00:41:13.380
Say it quickly.
快点说。

897
00:41:13.720 --> 00:41:15.100
Guys, and here's what you have to say.
伙计们，你们得这么说。

898
00:41:15.140 --> 00:41:15.640
Formal chrysanthemuMs.
正式的菊花。

899
00:41:16.240 --> 00:41:18.380
That was my best effort, by the way.
顺便说一句，那已经是我尽力了。

900
00:41:18.800 --> 00:41:23.400
I mean, literally, Jen Salata had to come in the room and help me break it down.
我是说，真的，珍·萨拉塔不得不走进房间帮我把它拆解开。

901
00:41:24.240 --> 00:41:29.900
But try saying it quickly while you're like throwing it away like you have no problem saying
但试着快速说出来，就像随口一说那样，就像你毫无压力地在演讲中说出来一样，

902
00:41:29.900 --> 00:41:33.200
it in a speech where you're pleading to save your relationship.
在那场演讲里，你还在恳求挽回你们的关系。

903
00:41:33.800 --> 00:41:34.800
And you know what?
你知道吗？

904
00:41:34.980 --> 00:41:36.700
It wouldn't have worked any other flower.
换成别的花都不会有这种效果。

905
00:41:36.940 --> 00:41:38.240
That's the funniest flower.
那是最搞笑的花。

906
00:41:38.480 --> 00:41:39.400
It had to be that.
非它不可。

907
00:41:39.580 --> 00:41:40.200
I know.
我知道。

908
00:41:40.680 --> 00:41:45.300
Well, while this whole Andy and Angela scene is going on in the conference room, there's
嗯，当安迪和安吉拉在会议室里上演那一幕时，

909
00:41:45.300 --> 00:41:47.540
a flip side to what's happening.
事情还有另一面。

910
00:41:47.720 --> 00:41:49.500
It's everyone in the bullpen watching.
就是办公区里的每个人都在看。

911
00:41:50.020 --> 00:41:51.820
It was deleted for time.
这一段因为时长原因被删减了。

912
00:41:51.820 --> 00:41:52.760
It's so great.
太棒了。

913
00:41:52.920 --> 00:41:55.740
And I really feel like Phyllis summed up the whole moment perfectly.
我真的觉得菲利斯完美地总结了那一刻。

914
00:41:56.980 --> 00:41:58.460
Phyllis, why is it taking so long?
菲利斯，为什么这么久还没出来？

915
00:41:59.220 --> 00:42:02.780
He found out his little angel's been screwing the beet farming weirdo.
他发现他的小天使一直在和那个种甜菜的怪胎鬼混。

916
00:42:02.920 --> 00:42:04.880
He's trying to make it make sense in his brain.
他正在努力让自己的大脑接受这个事实。

917
00:42:04.880 --> 00:42:07.180
And then he's going to come out here and kill you.
然后他就会出来杀了你。

918
00:42:09.060 --> 00:42:09.920
Thank you, Phyllis.
谢谢你，菲利斯。

919
00:42:10.260 --> 00:42:10.740
You're welcome.
不客气。

920
00:42:11.280 --> 00:42:11.820
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

921
00:42:11.840 --> 00:42:12.520
She got it.
她抓住了精髓。

922
00:42:13.020 --> 00:42:16.280
I mean, that made me laugh really hard.
我是说，那真的让我笑得很大声。

923
00:42:16.500 --> 00:42:17.860
I wish it had stayed in.
真希望那段没被剪掉。

924
00:42:19.180 --> 00:42:21.000
Well, this takes us to corporate.
好了，现在转到总公司那边。

925
00:42:21.600 --> 00:42:23.600
Andy and Angela are going to stay in the conference room.
安迪和安吉拉还要留在会议室里。

926
00:42:23.740 --> 00:42:24.420
They're not done.
他们还没完事。

927
00:42:24.580 --> 00:42:26.700
But meanwhile, we cut over to corporate.
但与此同时，镜头切到了总公司。

928
00:42:26.700 --> 00:42:29.920
And we see the reason why David Wallace has called Michael in.
我们看到了大卫·华莱士叫迈克尔过去的原因。

929
00:42:30.120 --> 00:42:34.420
He says to Michael, Scranton is outperforming the other branches.
他对迈克尔说，斯克兰顿分公司的业绩超过了其他分公司。

930
00:42:34.760 --> 00:42:36.240
Everyone else is struggling.
其他人都很挣扎。

931
00:42:36.460 --> 00:42:39.820
And we want to know, what are you doing right?
我们想知道，你到底做对了什么？

932
00:42:40.300 --> 00:42:43.560
What is Michael doing so right?
迈克尔到底做对了什么？

933
00:42:43.920 --> 00:42:48.920
I mean, everything in Michael lit up like a Christmas tree.
